    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d242">

                <pb facs="0374" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg286"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123C11/316: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-05-06T15:00:00-04:00">May 6, 1933—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. For Caffery from Phillips.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d242-f1"/> The President has
                    in mind appointing you Ambassador to Cuba on the termination of Sumner Welles’
                    period of ambassadorship there, which may be in about 3 months’ time. Welles
                    will then return to the State Department and resume his position of Assistant
                    Secretary. Meanwhile, we should like to have you fill the vacancy here of
                    Assistant Secretary. In this way you can become conversant with Cuban affairs
                    and be of general assistance to the Department.</p>
                <p>Please let me know whether this arrangement is agreeable to you.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d242-f1" n="16" xml:id="d242-f1-content">
                <p>William Phillips, Under Secretary of State.</p>
